Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; Mission: Humanity boot-gate registry key (RE'd 2026-07-25, docs/cd-check.md).
;
; The game's entire boot body (llm_boot_progress_draw, EN 0x004c3c53) sits inside
;   if (RegOpenKeyExA(HKLM\SOFTWARE\Techland\Mission Humanity) != NULL) { ... }
; so with NO key the function returns having done nothing and the game NEVER boots -- it
; pops a blank "Ok" modal and hangs before presenting its first frame. ONLY THE KEY'S
; EXISTENCE is load-bearing; the individual values are optional (none of the three
; RegQueryValueExA return codes is tested). SrcPath defaults to "Setup", Lang keeps the
; built-in variant, DestinationPath is never read (installer bookkeeping).
;
; A 32-bit game reading HKLM\SOFTWARE\... is redirected by WOW64, hence WOW6432Node.
;
; This is a REQUIRED bootstrap step on any fresh machine (a full game installer would
; create it; a hand-copied game tree does not). Import with an ELEVATED shell:
;   reg import tools\data\mh_registry.reg
; or apply it from tools/provision_rig.py (which does this + builds mh.focus.exe + deploys mh.dll).

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\WOW6432Node\Techland\Mission Humanity]
"SrcPath"="Setup"
"Lang"="English"
"UserID"="0"
"DestinationPath"="C:\\Games\\MH"
